{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>But on the tenth of the month.</b> What is the meaning of 'but'? Since all other festivals are called 'a holy convocation' — to eat and drink and rejoice — and this one is forbidden in all of these, therefore it writes 'but,' to teach that it is not called 'a holy convocation' except to honor the day, to offer a sacrifice, and to forbid it in labor — 'but you shall afflict your souls on it, for it is the Day of Atonements.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:22.716815190Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}